cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "authorecon: bibliographic reconciliation and submission hygiene"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vincent
    family-names: Gonzalez
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3640-014X"
    email: vincegonzalez@me.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/zengineco/apriori"
abstract: >-
  Two things a research programme needs and rarely has. `authorecon` reconciles
  what Zenodo, Wikidata, OpenAlex and the OEIS each record about the same body
  of work and reports where they disagree, which is how a self-citation
  masquerading as an external one gets caught. The `tools/` directory holds the
  gates: `submission_scrub.py` refuses to let a manuscript reach an editor with
  agent artifacts or stray comments still in the source; `slop_scan.py` looks
  for the structural habits that read as machine-written — contrastive pairs,
  announced candour, padded triads, restatement openers, em-dash density —
  which a word-list scan cannot find; and `software_inventory.py` reports
  licence, citation metadata and per-module documentation state across a set of
  repositories, so the gap between a script and something citable is a list
  rather than an impression.
keywords:
  - bibliographic reconciliation
  - research software
  - ORCID
  - Zenodo
  - Wikidata
  - OpenAlex
  - submission hygiene
  - research metadata
